 "_comment": [
  "The taxonomy for text_embeds_b16ft.json, one entry per species, index-aligned with that",
  "file's `species` array. Identical to taxonomy_b16.json in every label: the b16-ft head carries",
  "the same sixteen species, so the genus roll-up `src/confidence/taxonomy.ts` performs over them",
  "is the same tree. Only the head and engine change, because only the encoder behind it does.",
  "Every rank above genus is a SUM over its species, so a rare species cannot split its",
  "genus across rows. Kept beside the head rather than inside it: the head is a fitted",
  "artefact, and editing it to add 16 labels would bury that under a formatting diff."
